              "vo": "Think back to onboarding day. Alongside your badge and tax papers, HR handed you one extra sheet: open a checking account at this specific bank to receive pay. Sending money across town to other banks is technically easy; one batch file can pay dozens of banks at once. Putting the whole company under one bank simply lowers transfer fees, cuts down on bounced wires, and leaves finance with one tidy statement to check. That onboarding form was message number one: your company told the bank to add another worker to payroll, and the bank opened your checking account. Zero cash moved that day. But that piece of paper opened a monthly pipeline straight into the bank's books.",
