              "visual": "Deep underground view showing an external interbank settlement channel activating: a glowing transaction packet travels across town to an external bank.",
              "vo": "What if you insist on getting paid at a different bank across town? Then the transfer becomes Off-Us. The payment instruction has to travel out through an interbank clearing switch to reach your bank. That electronic message arrives in seconds, so your bank can credit your screen almost right away. Real money catches up later during central bank settlement, where banks net thousands of opposing payments together. Only when pay goes Off-Us does corporate money actually walk out of the payroll bank's vault. And for your employer, every outside transfer can tack on a fee — 3,300 dong per check in our example. Across hundreds of workers, those tiny wire fees add up fast, which gives finance teams one more reason to keep staff on one bank.",
              "onScreen": "Off-Us: message first · interbank settlement later · Fee example: 3,300 VND\nSFX: Short routing pulse"
