              "p": "A 0% contract rate guarantees only one thing: nominal payments sum to the sticker price (12 × 1,000,000 = 12,000,000 VND). It says nothing about the time value of money. Money paid a year from now costs less than cash parted with today, so comparing offers requires [[discounted cash flow|dcf]] analysis. Whenever upfront cash buys the same phone for 11,400,000 VND (example), paying 12,000,000 VND over twelve months embeds a real 600,000 VND financing cost."
