        "srtText": "1\n00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,720\nSame 50,000 VND morning coffee sitting on the counter.\n\n2\n00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:14,410\nWhy does tapping a credit card cost the shop 2.2%, while scanning a plastic QR stand pays 100% in three seconds flat?\n\n3\n00:00:15,490 --> 00:00:24,960\nWhen you tap a credit card, the POS terminal sends a pull instruction to advance money from your issuing bank for 45 days, triggering interchange fees.\n\n4\n00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:29,730\nScanning QR pushes cash straight out of your existing CASA checking balance.\n\n5\n00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:35,880\nNo bank advances a 45-day loan or absorbs default risk, so standard transfer fees drop to zero.\n\n6\n00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:42,090\nPre-funded interbank collateral lets the shop's bank credit the full 50,000 VND to Account 112 right away.\n\n7\n00:00:42,970 --> 00:00:46,450\nCommercial banks never ship cash for individual 50,000 VND coffees all afternoon.\n\n8\n00:00:46,450 --> 00:00:51,810\nMillions of two-way transfers offset each other, moving just one net reserve difference at the Central Bank at session close.\n\n9\n00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:57,670\nAcross 10,000,000 VND in daily cafe sales, cards return 9,780,000 VND two days later.\n\n10\n00:00:57,670 --> 00:01:03,340\nQR keeps the extra 220,000 VND at the counter while holding cheap 0.1% CASA deposits inside banks.\n\n11\n00:01:04,260 --> 00:01:09,100\nAt familiar neighborhood counters, scanning QR helps shops keep every dong.\n\n12\n00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:16,130\nWhen ordering from unfamiliar remote sellers online, remember QR works like cash with zero Chargeback rights.\n"
